     "notes": {
      "text": "2.c4, the Queen's Gambit, is the main line. It offers the flank c-pawn: if Black takes it, the d-pawn is pulled away from the centre and you can win the pawn back later, so most players decline it. 2.Nf3 and 2.Bf4 (London) are calmer; 2.e4?! (Blackmar-Diemer) cannot keep a pawn on e4 and is dubious.",
      "credit": {
       "source": "Wikibooks, Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5",
       "url": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Chess_Opening_Theory/1._d4/1...d5",
