     "notes": {
      "text": "Black has taken the pawn but no longer controls e4. 3.e3 opens the way for your bishop to take back on c4. 3.Nf3 (the classical line) and the ambitious 3.e4 are also good, while 3.Nc3 looks misguided. If Black tries to hold the pawn with ...b5, a4 attacks the pawn chain at its base.",
